&#x201C;Michael&#x201D; director Antoine Fuqua has been accused of assault, battery and intentional infliction of emotional distress by a Los Angeles bar manager following an incident back in February during which Fuqua allegedly pulled a gun on and struck the employee in the head.

In a 10-page civil claim filed Friday in the Los Angeles Superior Court, William Rosenthal, an assistant manager at the bar Good Times at Davey Wayne&#x2019;s, is said to have denied entry to Fuqua, his son, Brando, and his daughter because they were &#x201C;visibly overly intoxicated.&#x201D; Rosenthal was then spat on by a member of the group, to which Rosenthal told them they needed to leave the bar. An hour later, Fuqua accused Rosenthal of pepper-spraying his daughter, and when the manager denied the allegation, Fuqua &#x201C;pulled out a handgun&#x201D; and &#x201C;struck&#x201D; Rosenthal in the face. Fuqua then &#x201C;directed a racial and antisemitic slur&#x201D; and &#x201C;threatened to kill him.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Cannes Condemns Five-Year Prison Sentence Against Iranian Palme d’Or Winner Jafar Panahi and Pleads for International Support

&#x201C;As Plaintiff staggered back in pain, Defendant Brando Fuqua, appeared and approached Plaintiff and forcefully swung a handgun at Plaintiff&#x2019;s face,&#x201D; read the complaint. &#x201C;Defendants Antoine Fuqua and Brandon Fuqua then pointed their handguns at Plaintiff, placing him in imminent fear for his life, before fleeing down the street.&#x201D;

Rosenthal is seeking $50,000 as a result of his suffering &#x201C;serious physical and psychological injuries&#x201D; which include a nose fracture, head injury, skin lacerations, post-traumatic stress disorder, severe emotional distress and severe scarring, all of which continue to cause him &#x201C;great physical and mental pain and suffering.&#x201D; The claim noted that Rosenthal believes said injuries &#x201C;will result in some permanent disability.&#x201D;

The 100th Macy&#x2019;s Thanksgiving Day Parade is just two days away. Each year, thousands line the streets and millions more tune in around the country to watch the iconic balloons, floats and performers parade through New York City. Titled &#x201C;The Greatest Celebration,&#x201D; this year&#x2019;s event promises to go all out, featuring more balloons and brand-new floats among the festivities.

It takes months of preparation and a village of creatives working behind the scenes to bring everything together. Variety has spent the last few months speaking with the team behind the magic and going inside the epic operation of the Macy&#x2019;s Thanksgiving Day Parade. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Cannes Condemns Five-Year Prison Sentence Against Iranian Palme d’Or Winner Jafar Panahi and Pleads for International Support

The floats are built in New Jersey at Macy&#x2019;s Studios in Moonachie. The costumes and balloons are designed and also built. As the countdown begins, the balloons are tested, the rehearsals go into full effect and the finishing touches are added to the floats, while organizers appeal to the weather gods. But this is a well-oiled machine of artists who come prepared for the occasion. The parade debuted in 1924. This year, as it celebrates its 100th edition, Brendan Kennedy, director of creative production at Macy&#x2019;s Studio, explains the heart of the parade begins with one thing: &#x201C;storytelling.&#x201D;

When Variety caught up with Kennedy, he was already knee-deep in the design process and counting down to the big day. At this stage of planning, Kennedy and his team were collaborating with new partners and finalizing designs. The floats and balloons were in various stages of development &#x2014; some still in the concept phase.

&#x201C;This time last year, I was starting on our first balloon for this year and we&#x2019;ve been chipping away at that design-wise,&#x201D; Kennedy explains. &#x201C;This is just one part of the parade. There are so many aspects to it.&#x201D; Kennedy noted that the team constantly pushes the boundaries of creativity, and this year is no exception. &#x201C;Some classic characters are returning to the parade this year, which everyone will be super pumped for,&#x201D; he says. Among them are Underdog, the Macy&#x2019;s All-Stars Float and Sorcerer&#x2019;s Apprentice Mickey.

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s a massive deal for the folks at Disney,&#x201D; Kennedy says. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s not an IP that generally comes out, except for a huge celebration. It&#x2019;s our 100th parade, and they were really excited to join us. It was just a joy to get close to Mickey, but the Sorcerer&#x2019;s Apprentice is so special. It&#x2019;s that next level of elevated magic that blends really well with Macy&#x2019;s.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Kennedy also revealed that he and his team had been working on the Tony Sarg and the All-Stars float since the beginning of the year. Sarg, considered the godfather of American puppetry, designed the first six floats for the parade back in 1927.

This year, an entire Macy&#x2019;s float will be dedicated to Sarg and his creations.

&#x201C;There will be cold air inflatables, sculpts and puppets. It all takes place in this marionette theater where Tony Sarg himself is also represented as a marionette puppet,&#x201D; Kennedy explains. &#x201C;We&#x2019;re still working on how the character comes across, but we are collaborating with Puppet Heap to bring those stories to life in a few interesting ways.&#x201D; Kennedy acknowledges that not everyone may recognize Sarg&#x2019;s name, which is why spotlighting him is so important. &#x201C;This is the magician who brought us giant balloons,&#x201D; he says.

Another highlight is Snoopy, who returns to the parade in a new role as Joe Cool. &#x201C;Joe Cool is what happens when Snoopy is pretending to be a student at school. He&#x2019;s never been in the parade before in this form, which makes it really fun,&#x201D; Kennedy said. &#x201C;We&#x2019;re excited to bring him and Woodstock together. I was on the Parade Studio floor yesterday and saw an arm and an ear being worked on.&#x201D;

PJ Portera, the parade&#x2019;s concept artist and specialist, is responsible for designing this year&#x2019;s floats.

By July, Portera had already completed three and a half float designs, which were in various stages of production. &#x201C;Those are all done on my end,&#x201D; Portera says. &#x201C;They&#x2019;re on the floor now in different stages of production.&#x201D; He also worked on one main balloon and a smaller one, both currently in production. &#x201C;I&#x2019;m doing pretty great for July 30,&#x201D; he adds. Once a partner signs on, Portera and his team meet with them to brainstorm ideas. &#x201C;They give us an idea of what they&#x2019;re looking for &#x2014; whether it&#x2019;s for a balloon or a float &#x2014; and we start with rough sketches, throwing ideas at the wall to see what sticks.&#x201D; Afterward, the designs are reviewed by the engineering team to ensure feasibility before a final design is approved.

Portera also oversaw the return of Doodlebug, a legacy float from the 1968 Macy&#x2019;s Thanksgiving Day Parade. &#x201C;We&#x2019;ve been working on that for a while, even before the 2025 parade,&#x201D; he says, tracing the design process back to February 2025. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s a 100-foot-long caterpillar-type float with room for someone to sit on top.&#x201D; The idea came from John Chaney, a carpenter celebrating his 50th parade this year. &#x201C;John has a huge history with the parade, and that&#x2019;s where the Doodlebug idea was planted,&#x201D; Portera explains. His approach was to look at previous versions and decide how closely to stay true to the original design while incorporating modern updates. Portera worked closely with the engineering team to ensure the design was feasible.

&#x201C;I had to ask, &#x2018;Is this something that works in 2026 and what would it look like logistically to bring it to life?&#x2019;&#x201D; he says. Weather was also a significant consideration. &#x201C;We had to ensure the designs could withstand snow and rain. A lot of that falls to engineering.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

With just 70 days to go, costume designer Kimberly Montgomery was in the thick of preparations.

This year&#x2019;s parade will feature over 5,000 costumes. &#x201C;Our goal is getting everything into production in these final days and ensuring everything is delivered on time,&#x201D; Montgomery says. &#x201C;When the costumes come in, it&#x2019;s the most exciting part. It feels like Christmas when everything starts rolling in.&#x201D;

Montgomery emphasized the importance of designing costumes that accommodate Macy&#x2019;s employees, their friends and family members, who will wear them during the parade. &#x201C;We have to make sure the costumes are comfortable for everyone, no matter their shape, size, height or weight.&#x201D;

As with every department, weather is a major factor, especially when it comes to costumes. &#x201C;We have to consider whether the costumes are washable and if they can withstand rain,&#x201D; Montgomery says, recalling the time in 2024 when it poured.

&#x201C;Everything in the warehouse was dripping wet when it came back the Friday after Thanksgiving. We&#x2019;re ready for that if it happens again.&#x201D;

Montgomery shares the enthusiasm of designing the costumes for the Tony Sarg float. The clown costumes, inspired by his designs, are brightly colored and reminiscent of the 1920s. She also oversees the 100 balloon handlers&#x2019; costumes, which involve collaboration with licensing teams to ensure accurate designs.

Montgomery&#x2019;s parade day starts at 4:15 a.m. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s a well-oiled machine,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;We hire 200 to 250 people just for parade day to help dress everyone. Each person gets a picture of what the costume should look like, and then it&#x2019;s go time!&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

With less than 20 days to go, Kennedy is in Herald Square, preparing to flight-test all the new balloons. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s the first time outdoors,&#x201D; he reveals. The floats are still receiving their finishing touches ahead of the Nov. 17 press preview.

&#x201C;There&#x2019;s a lot of talent logistics going on,&#x201D; Kennedy adds. Performers, including singer and songwriter EJAE, are rehearsing for their big day and the team is working closely with NBC to ensure the televised show is a hit.

Billy Brightpaw will be making her debut as a featured balloon. &#x201C;Billy Brightpaw is an all-new IP,&#x201D; Kennedy explains. &#x201C;You can get her as a plush, on ornaments, on jackets &#x2014; she&#x2019;s everywhere. She&#x2019;s also going to be a live experience in Macy&#x2019;s Herald Square, where you&#x2019;ll be able to interact with her as a puppet. We&#x2019;re launching that on Black Friday.&#x201D;

Kennedy is still most excited about the Tony Sarg float. &#x201C;It came out so beautifully. It&#x2019;s one of the most stunning things we&#x2019;ve ever done,&#x201D; he says. &#x201C;The float has these amazing giant inflatables and a patina paint finish that really celebrates the history. The puppets we&#x2019;ve been working on truly make it come alive. Seeing them in action for the first time &#x2014; it&#x2019;s like your brain shuts down, and you&#x2019;re just a kid watching &#x2018;Sesame Street.&#x2019;&#x201D;

With the massive success of &#x201C;Minions and Monsters&#x201D; at the box office earlier this year, Buckaroo Bob the Minion will make an appearance. It&#x2019;s a playful nod to &#x201C;Dr. Strangelove.&#x201D; The float features Bob the Minion wearing a cowboy hat and riding the biggest banana the parade has ever seen. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s a feat of modern science and technology, but also very silly,&#x201D; Kennedy smiles. &#x201C;People are going to love it.&#x201D;

A new Purina Float will feature puppet dogs. Kennedy shares, &#x201C;The puppetry on this float is so clever, requiring someone to operate the dog from underneath the porch. It&#x2019;s a great example of how we&#x2019;re continuing to bring unexpected elements to the parade.&#x201D;

The DoorDash float recognizes the new partnership between the store and the delivery service. The team created a float that tells the story of quick delivery. &#x201C;It includes a mini Macy&#x2019;s,&#x201D; Kennedy says. There are also hidden stories, and in an elaborate design move, it features a moving ride. He says, &#x201C;The ride, which looks like a delivery vehicle, latches onto a track and circles the float. Kids will be riding in it, and it was a huge accomplishment to include a ride on a float.&#x201D;

The Macy&#x2019;s All-Stars Float will also feature a live performance by K-pop singer RiSe. &#x201C;It should be a wild moment,&#x201D; Kennedy teases. &#x201C;This float really pays tribute to the amazing parades that came before us while celebrating the characters people know and love.&#x201D;

As for 2027, Kennedy is already thinking ahead. &#x201C;People are knocking down the door to be part of this celebration,&#x201D; he says. &#x201C;The answer is always about marching forward and looking up.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid4' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

EXCLUSIVE: Greg Hovanessian ( The Mist , Cardinal) and Lindsey Normington ( Margo&#x2019;s Got Money Troubles , Anora ) are set to lead the new psychological thriller Nightwaves , from writer and director Kristian McKay ( Do Not Open , Kill Trip ) and Obscura Film . Cherie Currie ( Foxes , Twilight Zone: The Movie ) and Shane Coffey ( Pretty Little Liars , Good Girls ) will also star.

Set against the dark, desolate highways of Texas, Nightwaves &#xA0;unfolds over the course of a single night, following Mason (Hovanessian), a young man driving alone whose unexpected phone conversation with a mysterious woman (Normington) offers an initially welcome escape. As their exchange shifts from flirtation to increasingly unsettling questions, the woman on the other end of the line begins to threaten everything Mason is desperately trying to leave behind. With each passing mile, he finds himself moving closer to a confrontation he cannot simply hang up to avoid. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Casting Jillian Moray Sets Directorial Debut 'Pismo,' Stars Opposite Nuha Jes Izman, Madeline Popovich & More News 'Hunger Games: Sunrise On The Reaping' Heading To Potential Franchise-Record Monday With $12M

Currie and Coffey's roles are under wraps. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Production is currently underway in San Antonio and the surrounding Texas landscape.

&#x201C;There&#x2019;s something incredibly intimate about talking to someone in the dark when you can&#x2019;t see their face. You start filling in the blanks, and that can be seductive or terrifying,&#x201D; shared McKay. &#x201C;With Nightwaves , I want the audience to feel that connection tightening until it becomes a trap. Greg and Lindsey bring the vulnerability and unpredictability these roles demand, and having Cherie and Shane in this world gives the film such a distinct personality.&#x201D;

Obscura Film touts in a release how "McKay will bring a distinctive visual approach to the thriller, allowing tension and performances to unfold in extended, uninterrupted moments. Using the empty stretches of highway, passing headlights, and the confined interior of a moving car, the film transforms an ordinary phone conversation into an increasingly claustrophobic psychological experience, where what remains unseen may be more terrifying than anything in view." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The film is produced by Obscura Film partners Daunesh Alcott and McKay, alongside Jose Corres. Executive produced by Gustavo Oliveira.

Nightwaves expands Obscura Film&#x2019;s growing slate of independently produced genre features. The project follows Kill Trip , acquired by Quiver Distribution and released in 2026, and Do Not Open , McKay&#x2019;s supernatural thriller starring Freddy Carter, Lulu Wilson, Mark McKenna, John Ford Coley and Stelio Savante, which is currently in post-production.

Hovanessian is repped by Robert Stein Management and Clear Talent Group. Normington is repped by Innovative Artists and Authentic Talent & Literary Management. Coffey is repped by Industry Entertainment and Pakula/ King.

Adam Driver and Steven Soderbergh didn't get paid for the two-and-a-half years they spent developing " The Hunt for Ben Solo ," a standalone "Star Wars" movie that would've centered on Driver's fan favorite character Kylo Ren/Ben Solo. The actor said on the "Talk Easy" podcast that money was not even top of mind since they were given the upmost assurance from then-Lucasfilm president Kathleen Kennedy that the movie would happen, and thus the pay of it all could be figured out once it was greenlit. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 8 Standout Moments From the Governors Awards: Glenn Close Finally Gets Her Oscar, Diane Warren Pitches Olivia Wilde a Christmas Song and More 'Hold Onto Me' Director Myrsini Aristidou Kicks Off Historic Oscar Campaign for Sundance Audience Award Winner: 'I Really Feel Like We're Underdogs'

&#x201C;We were gonna do a Ben Solo movie and that didn&#x2019;t happen. And we worked on it for a longtime," Driver said on the podcast. "Soderbergh did that for nothing, because we were given a lot of confidence. Like Kathy [Kennedy] said we have a 100% approval rate [from Disney]. We worked on it. No one&#x2019;s paying us to work on it. The only reason we were working on it was we fucking loved the idea, how we wanted to do it, and I loved that character. And that was it. That was our guiding principle. All the money stuff came later. We were trying to figure out how to make it cheap so they could let us do what we wanted to do. So that was kind of a bummer."

Driver revealed the existence of &#x201C;The Hunt for Ben Solo&#x201D; in an Oct. 2025 interview with The Associated Press , explaining how Disney executives pulled the plug on the project because they couldn&#x2019;t wrap their heads around the character coming back after he presumably died in 2019&#x2019;s &#x201C;Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I always was interested in doing another &#x2018; Star Wars ,&#x2019;&#x201D; Driver said at the time. &#x201C;I had been talking about doing another one since 2021. Kathleen [Kennedy] had reached out. I always said: &#x2018;With a great director and a great story, I&#x2019;d be there in a second.&#x2019; I loved that character and loved playing him.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In an AP interview earlier this month, Driver said it was "criminal" for Disney to scrap "The Hunt for Ben Solo" after also saying on &#x201C;The Rich Eisen Show&#x201D; around the same time that the project is officially dead and he has no interest in trying to revive it ("I think the ship has sailed though," Driver said).

&#x201C;For me it was: Steven Soderbergh wants to make a &#x2018;Star Wars&#x2019; film. What are we debating?&#x201D; Driver told AP. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s what it is. It&#x2019;s criminal. Or it felt criminal. We&#x2019;re all moving on. On to the next. And Steven already has something else that&#x2019;s one of the best things he&#x2019;s ever written.&#x201D;

Driver originally told the AP in 2025 that he loved &#x201C;The Hunt for Ben Solo&#x201D; script, calling it the &#x201C;standard&#x201D; of what a &#x201C;Star Wars&#x201D; movie &#x201C;should be&#x201D; and comparing it to the &#x201C;handmade and character-driven&#x201D; feel of &#x201C;The Empire Strikes Back.&#x201D; He added that Lucasfilm execs Kennedy, Dave Filoni and Cary Beck backed the project until Disney shut it down.

&#x201C;We presented the script to Lucasfilm. They loved the idea,&#x201D; Driver recalled. &#x201C;They totally understood our angle and why we were doing it. We took it to Bob Iger and Alan Bergman, and they said no. They didn&#x2019;t see how Ben Solo was alive. And that was that.&#x201D;

Kathleen Kennedy expressed her own frustration with Disney pulling the plug on the project during her Lucasfilm exit interview . Soderbergh told BK Mag soon after that he was not surprised to read about Kennedy's annoyances.

&#x201C;We were all frustrated,&#x201D; Soderbergh said. &#x201C;You know, that was two and a half years of free work for me and Adam and [writer] Rebecca Blunt. When Adam and I discussed him talking about it publicly, I said, &#x2018;Look, do not editorialize or speculate about the why. Just say what happened, because all we know is what happened.&#x2019; The stated reason was, &#x2018;We don&#x2019;t think Ben Solo could be alive.&#x2019; And that was all we were told. And so there&#x2019;s nothing to do about it, you know, except move on.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I&#x2019;d kind of made the movie in my head, and just felt bad that nobody else was going to get to see it,&#x201D; the director continued. &#x201C;I thought the conversation was strictly going to be a practical one&#x2014;where they go, what is this going to cost? And I had a really good answer for that. But it never even got to that point. It&#x2019;s insane. We&#x2019;re all very disappointed.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

